{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788225276,"nonce":"MhbZgfb3Cf8/TVx9dAbs/yRR/o8=","title":"git-bug pull produced FIVE unreadable merge commits; the whole store panicked until they were reset","message":"Found in session 11 (`65b03c2`), 2026-08-31, while pushing the bug store so BORGES would not be stranded again.\n\n\n`git push origin 'refs/bugs/*'` was rejected — the remote had bug work this box did not. `git-bug pull` merged it: 3 new bugs, 12 updated. Immediately afterwards **every git-bug command panicked**:\n\n```\nBuilding cache...\npanic: DFS failed\ngithub.com/git-bug/git-bug/entity/dag.read[...]  entity/dag/entity.go:169\ngithub.com/git-bug/git-bug/entity/dag.ReadAll[...] entity/dag/entity.go:321\n```\n\nNot the cache — deleting `.git/git-bug/cache` and rebuilding reproduced it exactly. The store was unusable: even `git-bug bug show \u003cid\u003e` fails, because it builds the full cache first.\n\n\nBisected from an empty ref set, adding one ref at a time (54 refs). **Five are unreadable:** `20e5cda`, `70ac258`, `96d9315`, `d2e1229`, `fbb2c59`. The other 49 load fine.\n\n**The decisive measurement: every one of the five has a two-parent merge head, and BOTH PARENTS OF ALL FIVE ARE INDIVIDUALLY READABLE.** Only the merge commits are not.\n\n```\n20e5cda head=df6b25d2  parents READABLE f0b31539 / c51b0868\n70ac258 head=26ef66be  parents READABLE 547e68de / 8bdbfd61\n96d9315 head=6d5af6ef  parents READABLE fb5ef4f8 / 686e7705\nd2e1229 head=11f8bec7  parents READABLE e7d203b5 / 2c530e1c\nfbb2c59 head=b6cf1df2  parents READABLE b011e6e2 / 98503f9d\n```\n\nSo **no data is lost** — every operation is present in one parent or the other. What is broken is the merge git-bug itself wrote. All five are exactly the bugs where BOTH SIDES HAD DIVERGED; the twelve updated bugs that were fast-forwards are all fine.\n\n`20e5cda`'s merge head equalled the value already on the remote, so **BORGES's git-bug produced the same breakage** — this is not specific to this box. Version here: `git-bug version: dev-f2070b5325`. All 54 entities are `version-4`; a format mismatch was ruled out.\n\nAn earlier bisect misattributed this to `20e5cda` alone and then \"proved\" all 17 of its commits unreadable. That was a confound: one bad ref in the set poisons every subsequent test, so nothing can be tested until the set is otherwise clean. Recorded because it is a cheap mistake to repeat.\n\n\nEach of the five was reset to the parent with MORE content. In every case that was the earlier-dated parent — the remote/BORGES side — because this box's bug store was well behind:\n\n| bug | kept | comments kept | dropped | comments |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `20e5cda` | `c51b0868` | 7 | `f0b31539` | 6 |\n| `70ac258` | `8bdbfd61` | 5 | `547e68de` | 3 |\n| `96d9315` | `686e7705` | 12 | `fb5ef4f8` | 8 |\n| `d2e1229` | `2c530e1c` | 7 | `e7d203b5` | 5 |\n| `fbb2c59` | `98503f9d` | 13 | `b011e6e2` | 10 |\n\nStore then healthy: 54 bugs, all readable.\n\n**Cost: the session-11 close of `70ac258` was on the dropped side and had to be re-posted.** Nothing else written this session was lost. **The dropped parents are listed above and are still reachable objects — nothing needs re-typing, it needs re-merging.**\n\n\n- The five bugs' dropped-side operations are recovered into their refs, or a decision is recorded that they are not worth recovering, per bug.\n- Whatever recovers them does NOT go back through `git-bug pull`'s merge on a diverged pair without checking the result reads — the merge is the thing that breaks.\n- A check exists that a bug store is readable AFTER a pull and BEFORE a push, so this is caught in the second it happens rather than three commands later. `git-bug bug \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261` is the whole test.\n- The remote's `20e5cda` still points at the unreadable merge `df6b25d2`; decide whether to force it back to a readable parent so BORGES is not left with a store that panics.\n\n\nNot our code. Upstream `git-bug` `entity/dag.read` / `ReadAll`. Worth checking whether a newer release fixes it before building any workaround here.","files":null}]}